## STYLE RULES

- English for body text. Spanish summary paragraph labeled "En español:" at the end of each section only if SPANISH SUMMARIES = yes.
- Define every industry term inline the first time. Never assume the reader knows it.
- Insight before data: lead with the implication, then the number. Never open a sentence with a raw figure.
- Every figure carries its fiscal year in company convention (FY03/2026). Never "recently."
- No em dashes. No standalone "likely"; use "consistent with" or "pointing to." No arrows between data points.
- No ratings, price targets, or buy/sell opinions.
- Depth over brevity. Tables where they carry the information better than prose.
- Currency: yen with unit stated; give USD conversion only if you state the rate used.
- Do not paste Japanese source text unless the original term matters. Translate and cite.
